===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|fakan|faką|piece, part|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|pāǵe-|to nail, fasten|lang=ang}}. Cognate with Old High German [[fah]] (German [[Fach]]), Old Saxon [[fak]] (Dutch [[vak]]), Latin [[pangere]]. 

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/fæk/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|g=n|pl=facu}}

# an [[interval]], a period or space of time, while; division
# period of five years, [[lustrum]]

